course: dictionary
lesson: 7490
title: One word, two animals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and possum is one of them. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «The Australian possum living in a roof is a different animal from the American opossum» tells you that the two animals have similar names but are not the same.
explain: A possum is a marsupial, an animal that carries its babies in a pouch. In Australia and New Zealand, a possum lives in trees and comes out at night. In the US, opossum or possum is a different animal, also with a pouch.
explain: Sometimes possum is part of a phrase. «When badly frightened, an opossum may play dead» shows you what «play possum» means: to pretend to be asleep or dead. The words around it give you the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well. If not, read the words around it again.
fact: A possum is a marsupial, an animal that carries its babies in a pouch.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a possum is an animal that lives in trees and comes out at night.
fact: In the US, «possum» is short for «opossum», which is a different animal.
fact: «Play possum» means to pretend to be asleep or dead.
fact: Healesville Sanctuary near Melbourne keeps only Australian animals, and it helps save Leadbeater's possum.
exercise: In Australia, what kind of animal is a possum? | A bird that sings at dawn | A fish that lives in rivers | *A pouched animal that lives in trees | A kind of tree that grows in deserts
exercise: «When badly frightened, an opossum may play dead.» What does «play possum» mean? | To run very fast | *To pretend to be asleep or dead | To climb trees at night | To carry babies in a pouch
exercise: «You're not in trouble, possum.» Who might say this, and why? | *Someone speaking kindly to a person they like | A farmer warning about a pest | A scientist counting animals | A bus driver checking tickets
test: In New Zealand, why are possums a problem? | They are found only in the US | They live under the sea | They sing so loudly at night | *They harm forests and birds
test: «Healesville Sanctuary near Melbourne keeps only Australian animals.» What does this tell you? | The sanctuary keeps only birds | The sanctuary keeps only sea animals | The sanctuary keeps only American animals | *The sanctuary keeps animals from Australia only
exam: What is the difference between an Australian possum and an American opossum? | Only the possum lives in trees | *They are different animals, though both carry their babies in pouches | Only the opossum has a pouch | The two are the same animal
